{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact combined head 720f228a1214ad8a299ddf9a4f3488d614350569, tree 904b062f8fd1e32439302a2a7c23725edb08f970, on builder/gs3-fh1-main863-owned-20261115, all 22 artifacts, for request e988ff98 under my promise 95b41266. This verdict names both implementations, as ruling a10d429d requires: GS-3 (request 3a4f6d1c, promise a187a745, report c2e0e684) and FH-1 (request c8b2f4f6, promise 1be80098, report d6e5a5ce). `gs review --prepare` resolved both bindings and both reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/scope/vitest.scale-files.ts`. Two frozen maps hold the original four owners with six cases and the moved nine owners with sixteen. One loop refuses an empty path, a duplicate path across both maps, and a count that is not a positive safe integer. `scopeScaleGroup` answers only `omit`, `moved` or `all` and throws for any other name.\n- `scripts/scale-selection.mjs`. The `all` rule keeps the exact family list of main 270dc8c7, the archive support pattern and `packages/replay/src/archive.ts`, plus the selection files. `scripts/scale-runner.mjs` is now a selection file, and so is the inventory. The `moved` rule takes the GS-1 families and the protected files. Main and any `all` match win over `moved`. All four original owners fall under the `all` families, so a change to an original owner can never select `moved`. The moved owner `test/floor-kept.test.ts` also matches the `packages/scope/test/floor` family and selects `all`. That choice errs toward more scale.\n- `scripts/scale-runner.mjs`. The mode is validated before the output directory exists. `omit` starts no child and writes nothing. The child receives `ARTROOM_SCALE_MODE` equal to the runner's mode, which replaces any inherited value. `scaleResults` takes owners and the expected total from the chosen group and refuses an unexpected, duplicate or missing owner, a wrong per-owner count, a wrong total, an incomplete case and disagreeing report totals.\n- `scripts/test.mjs`, `vitest.projects.mjs` and the three configs. `fixedStages` refuses an `include` that disagrees with the mode and passes the mode itself to the Native phase. `testOptions` refuses `omit` outside Native and `moved` outside Native and Scale. Ordinary `npm test` and the configs default to `all`. A leftover `ARTROOM_SCALE_MODE=run` now throws instead of running, which fails closed. The scale project keeps its Worker, setup, `maxWorkers: 2`, timeouts and deadline factor.\n- `.github/workflows/scale-tests.yml`. It adds a daily schedule at 05:00 UTC and passes `all` explicitly. Permissions stay `contents: read`.\n- `scripts/check-shared-helpers.mjs`. Only the four apps and examples pathspecs gain `:(glob)`, so `**/` matches zero directories and a direct child such as `examples/x.ts` is now scanned. The scan passed over 931 sources at the gated source.\n- FH-1: `.githooks/pre-commit`, `.githooks/commit-msg` and `scripts/pre-commit.mjs`. The pre-commit hook refuses a checkout without local Prettier, refuses unstaged differences in the formatter's selected JSON, runs `scripts/format-json.mjs` without `--write`, then runs the shared-helper check. It never writes the working files or the index. The commit-msg hook decodes the message as fatal UTF-8 and calls the exported `checkMessage`, so it copies no rule. Both hooks fail closed on any exception. The root `package.json` declares `\"type\": \"module\"`, so the extensionless commit-msg hook runs as ESM.\n- `scripts/git-hooks.test.mjs`. Four cases set `core.hooksPath` only with `git config --local` inside `mkdtemp` scratch repositories: unformatted JSON and its staged repair, subject, body and UTF-8 message rules, missing Prettier, and a local bytes helper against its shared import. `scripts/test.mjs` adds the owner to `nodeFiles`, which accounts for Node 200 against 195.\n- `docs/testing.md` and `docs/testing-reference.md`. The three answers, the precedence, the `judge.ts` example, the runner's refusals and the preflight steps match the code. The link to `testing-reference.md#scale-selection-in-the-review-gate` resolves to the heading at line 434.\n- Both notes. They state the remaining limits: the first `moved` gate wall time is unmeasured, the scripted 22 and 16 reports prove no real Scale case, and no hook activation or deployment follows.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 4b198d0f is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The 22 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 4b198d0f 720f228a`.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-gs3-fh1-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 39e1a545…, as the GS-3 note states. Its first line after the npm header names head 202611c7 and tree 8b31fa84 with 0 changed files. It reports 13 observed scope-scale modules, and its last line is \"gate passed\". `result.json` has SHA-256 cadbf406… and the selector control log 56df87d4…, as the note states. From 202611c7 to the head only the two notes change.\n- Control. The selector mutant that answers `all` for a moved-only path fails \"GS1-only paths select moved\" with actual `all`, expected `moved`. That failure is the direct assertion for the new answer.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 13 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. R/LP1 holds the slot, so I ran no tests, compilers or builds.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One inventory owns both groups, and the selector, configuration, runner and Native phase all read their files and counts from it. Precedence keeps the pre-GS1 rule intact, so `moved` only narrows the GS-1 additions. The hooks reuse the formatter, the helper check and `checkMessage`, so the hooks and the gate cannot drift apart.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The hooks only read and refuse, and nothing in this head activates them. One fact for the planner: `docs/testing.md` tells a reader to run `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`. That setting lives in the shared repository configuration, so it applies to every worktree at once, including the builder's. After activation, a checkout without `node_modules`, such as a notes-only worktree, cannot commit. The doc states both facts. Activation is an owner's decision and not part of this approval.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The two maps replace one, and `scopeScaleGroup` replaces the separate `run` and `omit` flags with one answer.\n\nQualifications that stand: the first gate that selects `moved` must report its Native wall time, and that result decides whether the policy stays. The daily schedule takes effect only when this head reaches origin main. This approval authorizes no push, landing, hook activation, deployment or publication. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c2e0e68412132225ba0c4b3a85d4cf6d324d5df2","binding":"assigned","head":"720f228a1214ad8a299ddf9a4f3488d614350569","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:95b41266ba2005209afef2b5d673773631dbbee7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a187a745e8debdfb4f546a159c7d3fd3566c8123\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1be80098072bfb87aed9bedef0046f5219e6a0f7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f62c24828648e4ae84ed654d984354873de9242","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:182d6b647152e960eaad7b44062cfccbf99debfe, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1f84fd879ad57dbc49b48f6baa693db5ce3c5f9b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:24934e25e4a6c6cd537b8f9cd7a732513f2c05aa, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2c1238810bd88ad84167175c97e416abda22eabd, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef